    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνιοχ-εύω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁν-</span></b> , poet. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνιοχέω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>act as charioteer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μὲν νόθος ἡνιόχευεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.103
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				23.641
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.319
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>direct, guide</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδαλίῳ . . ἁνιόχευεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aet.
					2
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἐμῆς ψυχῆς
			ἡ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				4
			</span></i>: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορὸν ἡ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.82a
			</span></i>.</div>
